","Rocky Mountains","Appalachian Mountains"],"s":{"index":3}},{"k":"truefalse","i":"Las Vegas is located in the state of California.","t":"Cities","e":"\ud83c\udfb0","f":"Las Vegas is in Nevada, in the Mojave Desert, and was founded in 1905.","a":false},{"k":"choice","i":"Death Valley, one of the hottest places on Earth, is mostly in which state?","t":"National parks","e":"\ud83c\udf21\ufe0f","f":"Death Valley's 56.7 \u00b0C reading from 1913 is the highest air temperature officially recognised by the WMO.","o":["Arizona","Nevada","Utah","California"],"s":{"index":3}},{"k":"text","i":"Which US city is home to the Space Needle?","t":"Landmarks","e":"\ud83d\uddfc","f":"The Space Needle was built for the 1962 World's Fair in Seattle.","s":{"accepted":["Seattle"]}}]},{"slug":"oceans-and-sea-life","title":"Ocean Deep","tagline":"Dive into reefs, currents and the creatures of the big blue.","emoji":"\ud83d\udc0b","gradient":["#0284c7","#312e81"],"categories":["nature","geo"],"countries":null,"difficulty":"Medium","minutes":4,"questions":10,"prompt":"True or false?","yes_label":"True","no_label":"False","sort":284,"items":[{"k":"number","i":"Roughly what percentage of Earth's surface is covered by ocean?","t":"Oceans","e":"\ud83c\udf0d","f":"The ocean holds about 97% of all the water on Earth.","s":{"value":71,"tolerance":3,"min":0,"max":100,"unit":"%"}},{"k":"multi","i":"Select all the sea animals that are mammals.","t":"Marine mammals","e":"\ud83d\udc2c","f":"Like all mammals, dolphins breathe air and feed their young with milk.","o":["Dolphin","Shark","Manatee","Octopus","Walrus"],"s":{"indices":[0,2,4]}},{"k":"choice","i":"What is the largest coral reef system in the world?","t":"Reefs","e":"\ud83e\udeb8","f":"The Great Barrier Reef, off Australia, stretches over 2,300 km and can be seen from space.","o":["Belize Barrier Reef","Great Barrier Reef","Red Sea Coral Reef","Ningaloo Reef"],"s":{"index":1}},{"k":"truefalse","i":"Starfish (sea stars) are a type of fish.","t":